(EXT. FIELD STATION - DAY) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.00 696.00 Tm
(MARA and DELACROIX come up the last of the slope, packs on,) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.00 684.00 Tm
(bent into the wind. Below them the road they walked is a) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.00 672.00 Tm
(thin grey line, going all the way down.) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.00 648.00 Tm
(The station: a prefab hut bolted to the rock, a radio mast) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.00 636.00 Tm
(guyed four ways, a fuel drum, a generator crouched under a) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.00 624.00 Tm
(tarp. Everything that can rattle, rattles.) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.00 600.00 Tm
(The hut door opens before they reach it.) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.00 576.00 Tm
(TEO, 20s, comes out in two jumpers and no coat. Thin. He has) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.00 564.00 Tm
(the look of someone who has rehearsed what to say to people) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.00 552.00 Tm
(and forgotten all of it.) Tj
1 0 0 1 266.40 528.00 Tm
(TEO) Tj
1 0 0 1 180.00 516.00 Tm
(You came.) Tj
1 0 0 1 266.40 492.00 Tm
(DELACROIX) Tj
1 0 0 1 180.00 480.00 Tm
(We said we would.) Tj
1 0 0 1 266.40 456.00 Tm
(TEO) Tj
1 0 0 1 180.00 444.00 Tm
(People say that on the radio. It's) Tj
1 0 0 1 180.00 432.00 Tm
(different, seeing it.) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.00 408.00 Tm
(He shakes Delacroix's hand, then Mara's, then Delacroix's) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.00 396.00 Tm
(again.) Tj
1 0 0 1 266.40 372.00 Tm
(MARA) Tj
1 0 0 1 180.00 360.00 Tm
(You're Teo.) Tj
1 0 0 1 266.40 336.00 Tm
(TEO) Tj
1 0 0 1 180.00 324.00 Tm
(I'm Teo. Sorry. Come in, it's) Tj
1 0 0 1 180.00 312.00 Tm
(warmer. It isn't, but it's out of) Tj
1 0 0 1 180.00 300.00 Tm
(the wind.) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.00 276.00 Tm
(The wind leans on all three of them. The mast answers it) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.00 264.00 Tm
